    "trigger_card_number": 26,
    "title": "LESSON 20: THE PEN- NOUNS",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "   Semua pekerja di perusahaan itu sudah",
          "   pulang.",
          "   = All the workers at that company have",
          "     gone home.",
          "",
          "peN- is meN- with the m changed to a p.",
          "It takes the same six shapes for the same",
          "reasons, and it turns a verb into the one",
          "who does it.",
          "",
          "   tulis  menulis  penulis  a writer",
          "   jual   menjual  penjual  a seller",
          "   beli   membeli  pembeli  a buyer",
          "   jaga   menjaga  penjaga  a guard",
          "   curi   mencuri  pencuri  a thief",
          "",
          "If you can build the meN- form, you have",
          "the peN- form already. Change one letter."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "The whole of this cluster is built that",
          "way. Take the root, build the verb, then",
          "swap the m for a p:",
          "",
          "   pimpin  memimpin  pemimpin  a leader",
          "   rawat   merawat   perawat   a nurse",
          "   nyanyi  menyanyi  penyanyi  a singer",
          "   main    bermain   pemain    a player",
          "",
          "A handful take a bare pe- with no nasal",
          "at all, and simply have to be learned:",
          "   pekerja, pelajar, petani, petugas,",
          "   pelanggan",
          "",
          "Whatever its shape, a peN- word always",
          "answers one question - who or what does",
          "this? Read the front of a long noun and",
          "the answer is usually waiting there."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "021",
    "trigger_word": "kesempatan",
    "trigger_card_number": 78,
    "title": "LESSON 21: THE KE-AN NOUNS",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "   Ini kesempatan yang baik untuk belajar",
          "   bahasa baru.",
          "   = A good chance to learn a new language.",
          "",
          "ke- at the front and -an at the back wrap",
          "a root into an abstract noun: the state",
          "of it, the fact of it, the whole of it.",
          "",
          "   sempat  kesempatan  a chance",
          "   hidup   kehidupan   life",
          "   mati    kematian    death",
          "   salah   kesalahan   a mistake",
          "   aman    keamanan    safety",
          "   takut   ketakutan   fear",
          "   kuat    kekuatan    strength",
          "",
          "The two halves always travel together.",
          "Neither one does this on its own."
        ]
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "This is the ending that makes an",
          "Indonesian newspaper look harder than it",
          "is. Strip the ke- and the -an and a word",
          "you know is sitting in the middle.",
          "",
          "   kebersihan   -> bersih   clean",
          "   kemungkinan  -> mungkin  maybe",
          "   kecelakaan   -> celaka   mishap",
          "   keadaan      -> ada      to be there",
          "",
          "A small group are verbs rather than",
          "nouns, and they mean to suffer it:",
          "",
          "   kehilangan  to lose something",
          "   kehabisan   to run out of something",
          "",
          "A long word that begins ke- and ends -an",
          "is a noun before you know anything else."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
